---
description: Cultural/naming-tradition scope rules
globs: ["**/names/**", "**/db/**", "**/seed*/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Do not add compositional (Chinese/Japanese/Korean) or circumstantial
  (Akan/Yoruba-style) name examples, seed data, or schema assumptions —
  out of scope until a dedicated v2 data model exists.
- Never hardcode "meaning" or "origin" as a single scalar assumption on a
  name — use the `name_enrichments` per-source/per-field shape so this
  stays extensible.
- Keep the `tradition_type` column/value on `names`. Don't remove it even
  though only `'etymological'` is populated now.
- If a change touches which cultures/languages are represented (UI
  defaults, examples, seed data), don't default to Western examples by
  habit — but don't fabricate low-confidence coverage either. Flag the gap
  in a comment instead of guessing.
